o continue contracting with foreign coaches."}, {"Q": "How many times have the Tunisian and Egyptian teams met in official and friendly matches?", "A": "39 times", "S": "The two teams have met 39 times in both official and friendly matches."}, {"Q": "Who is the most participating Tunisian in the tournament?", "A": "Youssef Msakni", "S": "Youssef Msakni is the most participating Tunisian in the tournament, he played 25 matches in 7 participations between 2010 and 2021."}, {"Q": "Who supplied the Tunisian national team with sports uniforms from 2002 to 2011?", "A": "The German company Puma.", "S": "From 2002 to 2011, the German company Puma started providing the Tunisian national football team kits since the 2002 FIFA World Cup."}, {"Q": "Did Tunisia qualify for the 2006 World Cup?", "A": "Yes", "S": "In the same year, the Tunisian national team played the World Cup qualifiers in 2006, and succeeded in overcoming Guinea (lost 2\u20131, win 2\u20130), Kenya (win 1\u20130, win 0\u20132), Malawi (draw 2\u20132, win 7\u20130), Botswana (win 4\u20131, win 1\u20133) and finally Morocco, which attracted them to a 2\u20132 draw in the last round at the Stade 7 November in front of 60,000 spectators, which enabled the Tunisian team to qualify for the fourth World in its history and the third in a row."}, {"Q": "Who was one of the most loyal fans of the Tunisian team?", "A": "Bechir Manoubi", "S": "He attended the team's matches worldwide since 1960, he was famous for wearing the Mexican hat and his suit with thousands of slogans and cards for the various events he covered."}, {"Q": "Who was the coach of Tunisia when they qualified for the FIFA World Cup in 1978?", "A": "Abdelmajid Chetali", "S": "At the same time, the team was able to qualify for the first time in the FIFA World Cup in 1978 after a remarkable performance in the qualifiers led by a distinguished generation such as Mokhtar Dhouib, N\u00e9jib Ghommidh, Raouf Ben Aziza and Tarak Dhiab."}, {"Q": "Who was the best player in the 2022 Kirin Cup Soccer?", "A": "Ferjani Sassi", "S": "In the semi-finals, Tunisia beat Chile 2\u20130 and then Japan 3\u20130 and thus won the title for the first time.Ferjani Sassi was named the tournament's best player, while his compatriot Issam Jebali finished top scorer with two goals."}, {"Q": "Who supplied the Tunisian national football team with sports uniforms in the 2002-2011 period?", "A": "The German company Puma.", "S": "From 2002 to 2011, the German company Puma started providing the Tunisian national football team kits since the 2002 FIFA World Cup."}, {"Q": "Who did Tunisia play in their opening match against Kenya?", "A": "Kenya", "S": "On 28 March 2009, Tunisia opened the qualifiers with a 1\u20132 victory in their opening match against Kenya."}, {"Q": "When was the first match at the Stade Mustapha Ben Jannet played?", "A": "On 7 July 2001", "S": "The first match at the stadium was played on 7 July 2001 against between \u00c9toile du Sahel and CS Hammam-Lif for the Tunisian Cup final."}, {"Q": "Who did Tunisia face in the 2021 Africa Cup of Nations qualification?", "A": "Tunisia faced Libya, Equatorial Guinea, and Tanzania.", "S": "The 2021 Africa Cup of Nations qualification are drawn, with Tunisia facing Libya, Equatorial Guinea and Tanzania."}, {"Q": "How many times has Tunisia participated in the African Cup of Nations?", "A": "20 times", "S": "Tunisia has participated in the African Cup of Nations 20 times and holds the record for the number of consecutive participations with 15 between 1994 and 2021."}, {"Q": "When did Tunisia gain independence from France?", "A": "20 March 1956", "S": "Tunisia gained independence from France on 20 March 1956."}, {"Q": "Who replaced Kasperczak as the coach of Tunisia's national team?", "A": "Francesco Scoglio", "S": "Kasperczak was sacked and replaced with the Italian coach Francesco Scoglio, who qualified the team for the 2000 Africa Cup of Nations ideally after winning over Algeria, Uganda and 